          "settings": {
            "icon_type": "fontawesome",
            "icon_class": "",
            "heading": "Acne is an inherited disorder of the pore.",
            "text": "If you're prone to breakouts, your pores shed skin cells up to five times faster than normal. This buildup clogs your pores and creates the whiteheads, blackheads, and pimples you see on your skin."
          }
        },
        "value_prop_cGUrAU": {
          "type": "value_prop",
          "settings": {
            "icon_type": "fontawesome",
            "icon_class": "",
            "heading": "Here's the part most people don't realize:",
            "text": "acne takes 60-90 days to form under your skin before you ever see it. That means what you did last week isn't showing up on your face today — it's what happened 2-3 months ago."
          }
        },
        "value_prop_pVdTVN": {
          "type": "value_prop",
          "settings": {
            "icon_type": "fontawesome",
            "icon_class": "",
            "heading": "",
            "text": "This is exactly why quick fixes don't work. A single facial or a new product can't undo months of buildup overnight. And it's why random changes to your routine feel pointless — you're not seeing the results of what you're doing NOW, you're seeing the results of what you did months ago."
          }
        },
        "value_prop_KHX8Gb": {
          "type": "value_prop",
          "settings": {
            "icon_type": "fontawesome",
            "icon_class": "",
            "heading": "The good news? ",
            "text": "Once you understand how acne actually works, you can finally get ahead of it. With the right approach — consistent treatments, proper homecare, and eliminating hidden triggers — you CAN achieve clear skin. It just takes a system, not a single solution."
          }
        }
      },
